        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 22:10",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Now, my son, the Lord be with thee; and prosper thou, and build the house of the Lord thy God, as he hath said of thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 22:11",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Only the Lord give thee wisdom and understanding, and give thee charge concerning Israel, that thou mayest keep the law of the Lord thy God.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 22:12",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Then shalt thou prosper, if thou takest heed to fulfil the statutes and judgments which the Lord charged Moses with concerning Israel: be strong, and of good courage; dread not, nor be dismayed.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 158,
            "end": 165,
            "text": "TG Courage."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Courage.",
            "prettyString": "TG Courage",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Courage",
                "entryId": "tg-courage",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 22:13",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "Now, behold, in my trouble I have prepared for the house of the Lord an hundred thousand talents of gold, and a thousand thousand talents of silver; and of brass and iron without weight; for it is in abundance: timber also and stone have I prepared; and thou mayest add thereto.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 89,
            "end": 96,
            "text": "1 Chr. 29:4."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "1 Chr. 29:4.",
            "prettyString": "1 Chronicles 29:4",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "1chronicles",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 29,
                    "end": 29,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 4,
                        "end": 4
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 22:14",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "Moreover there are workmen with thee in abundance, hewers and workers of stone and timber, and all manner of cunning men for every manner of work.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 18
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 22:15",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Of the gold, the silver, and the brass, and the iron, there is no number. Arise therefore, and be doing, and the Lord be with thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 62
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 90
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 22:16",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "David also commanded all the princes of Israel to help Solomon his son, saying,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 79
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 22:17",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "Is not the Lord your God with you? and hath he not given you rest on every side? for he hath given the inhabitants of the land into mine hand; and the land is subdued before the Lord, and before his people.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2
          },
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 50
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Chronicles 22:18",
        "book": "1 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "Now set your heart and your soul to seek the Lord your God; arise therefore, and build ye the sanctuary of the Lord God, to bring the ark of the covenant of the Lord, and the holy vessels of God, into the house that is to be built to the name of the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 134,
            "end": 137,
            "text": "TG Ark of the Covenant."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
